==== Opening the case ====

//Main PCB://\\
{{media:billion:bipac_7700n_pcb.jpg?200|BiPAC 7700N}}

**Note:** This will void your warranty!


To open the device and access the main circuit board:

  - Flip the device onto it's back
  - Use a pin or the blade of a sharp knife to carefully prise up the black foam rubber feet (one in each corner)
  - Remove the four Phillips head screws (which you have now revealed,) by using a normal sized Phillips head screw driver
  - Flip the whole unit back over and then lift the top cover straight up vertically and it should come away cleanly from the rest of the body in one single piece
  - The circuit board can finally be accessed and even carefully lifted out if desired

Reassemble in the reverse order.


